<title>PORTUGAL: Escudo slides vs mark, seen extending losses.</title>
<headline>Escudo slides vs mark, seen extending losses.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The escudo followed the peseta lower against the mark and dealers expected it to extend losses over the session.</p>
<p>The escudo opened at 101.00/03 per mark after closing at 100.95/101.00 on Thursday but dealers saw support at 101.10.</p>
<p>&quot;Since the peseta is falling the Bank of Portugal will allow some depreciation in the escudo but it won't accept a rate below 101.10,&quot; said one dealer.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +(351-1) 3538254</p>
</text>
